 36CL    24MG(14N,2PG):XUNDL-2         2012AY04                           201209
 36CL c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2012Ay04:                          
 36CL2c  Phys Rev C 86, 024320 (2012)                                           
 36CL c  Compiled by E. Thiagalingam and B. Singh (McMaster); Sept 2, 2012      
 36CL c  {+14}N beam at E=31 MeV provided by the XTU-TANDEM accelerator of      
 36CL2c  Laboratori Nazionali di Legnaro. Target=1 mg/cm{+2} {+24}Mg (99.7%     
 36CL3c  enriched). Measured  E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g|g-coin, |g(|q), |g|g(|q),    
 36CL4c  Doppler-broadened line shapes using the 4|p-GASP array composed of     
 36CL5c  40 Compton-suppressed large-volume, HPGe detectors. Deduced levels, J, 
 36CL6c  |p, multipolarity, mixing ratio, B(M1), B(E2), half-lives. Comparison  
 36CL7c  with shell model calculations.                                         
 36CL cG $ Expected R{-ADO} values are 0.8 and 1.4 for |DJ=1, dipole, and       
 36CL2cG |DJ=2, quadrupole transitions, respectively.                           
 36CL cG $ Reduced transition probabilities in W.u. deduced by the compilers    
 36CL cL E$ From least-squares fit (by compilers) of E|g data                   
 36CL cL T$ From Doppler-shift attenuation method (2012Ay04), unless otherwise  
 36CL2cL indicated                                                              
 36CL cL T(A)$ From Adopted Levels of {+36}Cl in ENSDF database                 
